# AGENTS.md

## Project overview

`{{.Project}}` ({{.Module}}) was generated by
[gin-kit](https://github.com/Alfian57/gin-kit) — {{if eq .Edition "framework"}}framework edition: generic
HTTP and lifecycle behavior comes from the versioned gin-kit runtime; this
repository contains only application-owned code{{else}}starter edition: the runtime is vendored
into this repository under `internal/platform/` so every layer is visible and
editable{{end}}.

- Mode: `{{.Mode}}` · Database: `{{.Database}}` · Data access: `{{.ORM}}`
- Authentication: {{if .Auth}}enabled (JWT + refresh rotation){{else}}disabled{{end}} · Tasks example: {{if .Example}}enabled{{else}}disabled{{end}}

Keep the explicit flow:

```text
router -> handler (binds DTO, wraps response) -> service (DTO in, domain out) -> repository -> database
```

## Layout

- `internal/handler/` — HTTP handlers; bind with `httpx.BindJSON[T]` and
  friends, respond with `httpx.OK/Created/List/NoContent/Fail`.
- `internal/dto/` — transport shapes: `Create<Name>Request` /
  `Update<Name>Request` (validate tags + `Normalize()`) and `<Name>Response`
  with explicit `New<Name>Response` mappers.
- `internal/service/` — business rules; accept DTOs, return domain values,
  never import HTTP types.
- `internal/domain/` — models and repository interfaces.
- `internal/repository/` — {{.ORM}} persistence.
- `migrations/` — versioned goose SQL; `internal/database/seeders/` +
  `internal/database/factories/` — explicit seeder registry and model
  factories.
{{if eq .Edition "framework"}}- Runtime behavior (envelope, validation, security, lifecycle) comes from
  `github.com/Alfian57/gin-kit/framework`; customize through
  `framework.Options`, hooks, and middleware — never copy or edit gin-kit
  core.{{else}}- `internal/platform/` — vendored runtime copies (httpx, validation, query,
  config, database, factory{{if eq .Mode "ui"}}, session{{end}}); editable, but keep the HTTP
  contract stable.{{end}}

## Commands

```bash
gin-kit run                # serve with .env loaded
gin-kit check              # gofmt report + tests + vet (read-only)
gin-kit routes             # print the routing table
gin-kit generate resource <Name> --fields "title:string,done:bool" [--soft-delete]
gin-kit generate client --lang ts

# Personal API tokens persist only hashes and reveal plaintext once.
# Protect token routes with auth.RequireToken rather than JWT middleware.
gin-kit generate dto|domain|repository|handler|service|middleware|policy|factory|seeder|migration <Name>
{{if eq .Edition "framework"}}gin-kit generate job|event|mail <Name>
{{end}}gin-kit db up|down|status|redo|create|seed
gin-kit db reset --yes | fresh --yes   # destructive
{{if eq .Edition "starter"}}gin-kit upgrade [--diff] [--apply] [--force]   # refresh vendored internal/platform
{{end}}gin-kit doctor
gin-kit explain architecture|request-flow|database|auth|commands
```

Generators never edit existing files — they print the wiring snippet to
paste into `internal/app/app.go`.

## Rules

- Keep documentation and user-facing text in English.
- Pass `context.Context` through service and repository boundaries.
- Bind request DTOs in handlers; validation happens once, at bind time
  (`422 validation_failed` with `details.fields`, `400 invalid_json`,
  `413 body_too_large`). Do not re-validate in services — normalize there.
- Return response DTOs through their `New<Name>Response` mappers. Never add
  credential-like fields (password, secret, token, hash) to a response type.
- Preserve request IDs and the standard error envelope
  (`{"error": {code, message, details, request_id}}`) across new handlers.
{{if eq .Edition "framework"}}- Every route change updates the matching `Describe` call so the OpenAPI
  docs at `/docs` stay truthful.
{{else}}- Every route change updates `api/openapi.yaml` so the published contract
  stays truthful.
{{end}}- Put schema changes in `migrations/`; never use auto-migration in
  production code.
- Assign new endpoints to the general, auth, or expensive rate-limit class.
- Never trust forwarded client IP headers without an explicit
  `TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS` value.
- Add tests for new behavior (`apptest` drives handlers end-to-end; fakes
  implement the repository interfaces; factories build test data).
- Keep the project module path in `go.mod`; never replace it with the
  gin-kit module path.{{if eq .Edition "framework"}} Customize framework behavior through public
  options, hooks, middleware, and interfaces before forking the runtime.{{end}}
{{if .Example}}- Keep the Tasks example useful as a reference implementation.
{{end}}
## Documentation discipline

When you change behavior, update the affected documentation in the same
change: this file and `README.md` when the workflow changes,
{{if eq .Edition "framework"}}the `Describe` calls{{else}}`api/openapi.yaml`{{end}} when endpoints change, and
`.env.example` when configuration changes. A feature is not done until its
documentation exists.

Run `gin-kit check` before finishing any change.
